Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:34:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Stop passing `CC_OPT_FLAGS` to `--host_copt` in
 `configure.py`.

Passing `CC_OPT_FLAGS` (such as `-mcpu=apple-m1` on Apple Silicon) to `--host_copt` causes Bazel to forward target-specific CPU flags to all `exec` configurations, including `darwin_x86_64-opt-exec` host tool targets, which fails with `error: unknown target CPU 'apple-m1'`. Only write `CC_OPT_FLAGS` to `build:opt --copt`, matching XLA's `configure.py`.

Fixes #111876

PiperOrigin-RevId: 993943608
---
 configure.py | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure.py b/configure.py
index ffcfb82a519b0bfb1e4b02f2bdc50d0aba66dfbe..848253d83679f638455ee1be773d9b79e1101c35 100644
--- a/configure.py
+++ b/configure.py
@@ -472,7 +472,6 @@ def set_cc_opt_flags(environ_cp):
                                                  question, default_cc_opt_flags)
   for opt in cc_opt_flags.split():
     write_to_bazelrc('build:opt --copt=%s' % opt)
-    write_to_bazelrc('build:opt --host_copt=%s' % opt)
 
 
